    "answer": {
      "short": "They are the same because $\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^x=2^{-x}$.",
      "worked": "The curves are identical. By the law of negative indices,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^x&=(2^{-1})^x\\\\&=2^{-x}.\\end{align*}$$",
